    "standardized_narrative": "In 2017, Syndicate 623 released $39.7 million in prior year reserves, primarily driven by the consistent reserving philosophy of setting initial reserves with risk margins that are released over time as uncertainty reduces. Reserve releases were mostly derived from the 2010, 2013, 2014, and 2015 years of account, particularly within Specialty lines. While 2017 catastrophe activity (Hurricanes Harvey, Irma, Maria, Mexican earthquakes, and Californian wildfires) led to lower margins in affected areas, it did not cause an overall strengthening of prior year reserves, but rather reduced the rate of releases. The syndicate's robust reserve monitoring processes, including quarterly peer reviews and actuarial analysis, contributed to the identification of areas for release.",
    "raw_causal_phrases": [
      "consistent reserving philosophy, with initial reserves being set to include risk margins that may be released over time as and when any uncertainty reduces",
      "The margin held above the actuarial estimate was 5% at the end of 2017 (2016: 6.6%). This margin decreased in 2017 which was in part due to the catastrophe activity in the second half of the year, which resulted in much lower margins than usual in the affected areas.",
      "Reserve monitoring is performed at a quarterly 'peer review', which involves a challenge process contrasting the claims reserves of underwriters and claim managers, who make detailed claim-by-claim assessments, and the actuarial team, who provide statistical analysis. This process allows early identification of areas where claims reserves may need adjustment.",
      "reserve releases - mostly deriving from the 2010, 2013, 2014 and 2015 years of account - increasing to $21.8m"
    ],
